// annotations/MyDecorator.fol — package source file in package "annotations"
// Spec: language-ref.md > Annotations and Decorators, Builtin Directives
//
// A DECORATOR is a function: it takes a target, transforms it, and returns the
// transformed target. That is the difference from an annotation, which only
// carries data.
//
// The built-in decorator family includes @co.dap.before, @co.dap.after,
// @co.dap.around, @co.dap.callback, @co.dap.defer, @co.dap.event, and the
// execution decorators used in execution/Tasks.fol.

@co.dap.decorator
MyDecorator(target co.lang.function)->(co.lang.function) = {
    this.return target;
}
